    fact_sought: "which enum a variant spelling belongs to, which decides whether the variant renders as a qualified path",
    keys_on: "the bare variant name across every enum in every module of the closure",
    identity: AvailableUpstreamNotThreaded { nearest_holder: decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_emit_info", decl_name: "add_emit_item_summary") },
    outcome: AmbiguityDetectedThenAnswered { sentinel: "the empty string, written into the map when a second enum claims the same variant spelling", what_is_emitted: "rust_qualify_type_leaf_name reads the sentinel and emits the BARE variant name -- the ambiguity is computed, then widened away rather than refused" },
    reach: ReachedByMeasuredPopulation { measurement: "REACH RESTS ON THE COLLISION HALF, NOT ON THE CONNECTIVE SPECIMEN, and an earlier revision of this row had that backwards. WHAT HOLDS: colliding variant spellings are co-resident in the pool the required floor actually resolves (dag plus src/v2) -- Refused is declared by std.coercion TypeRealizationDecision, std.observation ObservationOutcome and v2.std.execution_surface ShellEmissionAuthorization; Unknown by std.encoding Encoding, std.reducible ReduceVerdict and v2.std.execution_surface AvailabilityFact -- so the sentinel is written and then read as a bare name in an invocation that runs on every PR. WHAT IS RETRACTED: this row briefly claimed a measured COLLAPSE at this HEAD, on the ground that Connective is declared by both v1.compiler.core and v2.std.node with Conj and Disj in each. Both declarations exist and the collapse is provable FROM THE FOLD IF THEY ARE CO-RESIDENT -- but on main no standard invocation puts them in one pool: regen resolves src/v1 plus dag (cli_run.rs regen_source_roots) and the floor resolves dag plus src/v2, so neither pool holds both. crisp-crab-430 ran the falsifier this carrier offered and it FALSIFIED the account: all 26 affected mirrors emit names absent from their main import lists, so suppression is not what keeps main quiet, and main positively emits the CORRECT line use crate::v1_std_core::Connective -- the synthesis path runs on main and answers right. The unmasking is CO-RESIDENCY, and on their branch it is caused by src/v2 being added to regen_source_roots. THE COROLLARY IS BIGGER THAN THE SPECIMEN AND IS WHY THIS ROW KEEPS IT: whether this fold sees one entry or two is a function of the INVOCATION rather than of the module graph, so every identity answer downstream of it is invocation-relative" },
